  "takeaways": {
    "uz": "Applied to Uzbekistan without any Uzbek data, the naive splice jumps ×4.32 at 2012, the KZ-harmonized series ×1.77, a locally refitted one ×1.24 (MODIS alone ×1.38). In 2012–2019 the KZ model is off by 31.2% a month and -28.6% in total; the same model refitted on Uzbekistan: 15.6% and -0.2%. Uzbekistan's VIIRS/MODIS ratio is ×3.34, the KZ model implies ×2.38: VIIRS sees relatively more fires there (C1: small agricultural burns). 2025 contains the new industrial source near 38.1°N 67.3°E (C2), so the holdout is also shown to 2024 — it changes little.",
    "tm": "The naive splice jumps ×3.48 at 2012, the KZ-harmonized series ×1.37, a locally refitted one ×1.15 (MODIS alone ×1.21). Overlap error as-is 26.0% (bias -13.9%), local refit 16.0%. 57% of Turkmenistan's confident detections are static sources (Kazakhstan 13%); FIRMS `type` removes them in archive data and the mask in recent data (precision/recall above). The remaining error is the same kind as Uzbekistan's: VIIRS/MODIS ×2.88 vs ×2.48 from the KZ model. TM's monthly R is the lowest of the cell-level countries.",
    "annual": "Kyrgyzstan and Tajikistan have only a few hundred fire cell-days a year, so only annual totals are meaningful. KGZ: annual error 14.9%, bias -14.0% (raw MODIS: -70%); TJK: annual error 13.6%, bias +9.6% (raw MODIS: -72%). The harmonized totals are usable for a yearly trend, not for single months.",
    "transfer": "Transfers as-is: KAZ, KGZ; does not: AUS, BRA, IND, PRT, TJK, TKM, USA, UZB. The observed VIIRS/MODIS ratio ranges from ×1.54 to ×4.46; the KZ model cannot know a country's ratio and errs in the direction of the difference (too high for Portugal, too low for India). Refitted locally, the same model gets 5.2–38.7% monthly error. Honest conclusion: the METHOD transfers across biomes, the COEFFICIENTS do not — every country needs its own 2012–2019 overlap fit (which FIRMS provides everywhere).",
    "ba": "Holding burned area fixed, naive: continuous (95% CI includes 1) in none; KZ-harmonized: continuous (95% CI includes 1) in KAZ; locally harmonized: continuous (95% CI includes 1) in KAZ, TJK, TKM, UZB. The naive series jumps ×1.8–×3.9 everywhere. Correlation with burned area is high in Kazakhstan and weak in Kyrgyzstan/Tajikistan (few fires; much burned area there is not seen as active fire).",
    "events": "Kostanay forest and steppe fires (Auliekol) (2022-09): 91 cell-days in one hexagon vs a normal of 1, rank 393 of 1183. Abai region forest fire (Semey Ormany) (2023-06): 123 cell-days in one hexagon vs a normal of 0, rank 231 of 1183. The top events are the largest local excesses; check them against news before the demo."
